Chapter: T3IsaPlug
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

Section: Body

 Two modes. IR-CCE is the plug proper: Codex IR in, T3ISA assembly out.
 T3-ASM runs only the encoder half, assembly in and words out, so the Codex
 encoder can be held to the same corpus the PowerShell one was proven
 against. Without that second entry the encoder would be reachable only
 through the emitter, and an instrument reachable only through the thing it
 measures is not an instrument.

  dispatch : Text -> [Console] Nothing
  dispatch (mode) = act
    source <- read-serial-cce mode
    let output = if mode == "T3-ASM" then encode-t3isa-asm source
                 else emit-from-ir source
    in print-line-uni output
  end

  emit-from-ir : Text -> Text
  emit-from-ir (source) =
   let parsed = parse-ir-chapter source
   in emit-t3isa-chapter (parsed.chapter) (parsed.type-defs)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    mode-result <- read-line-cce
    when mode-result
      is Just (mode) -> dispatch mode
      is None -> print-line-uni "no input"
  end
